CMD commands:
- set - check the path
- ver - system version
- systeminfo - info about system
- cls - clears page
- ipconfig - network information
- ipconfig /all - more info about network
- ping <target_name> - checks if we can access a network server
- tracert <target_name> - tracks the network route
- nslookup <target_name> - shows the IP adress
- netstat -abon - current connections and listening ports
- cd - current directory
- dir - child directories
- dir /a - also hidden directories
- dir /s - files in current directory
- tree - tree representation of files
- cd <directory> - changes directory
- cd .. - goes up one level
- mkdir - create directory
- rmdir - delete directory
- type - view file
- more - view bigger file
- copy <file> <new_file> - copies a file
- move <file> <location> - moves a file
- del <file> - deletes a file
- copy *.md - copies all files that are md
- tasklist - running processes
- tasklist /FI "imagename eq sshd.exe" - all processes related to sshd.exe
- taskkill /PID <task_id> - kills the process
- chkdsk - chcecks the file system for errors
- driverquery - list of all installed drivers
- sfc /scannow - scans system files for corruption

PowerShell commands:
- Get-Command - lists available commands
- Get-Command -CommandType "Function" - lists all commands that are functions
- Get-Help <cmdlet> - help about query
- Get-Help <cmdlet> -examples - common examples
- Get-Alias - list of available aliases
- Find-Module -Name "PowerShell" / -Name "Remove*"- searches for this module from online repositories
- Install-Module -Name "PowerShellGet" - we found a module and we want to install it now

